  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection of Vulnerable Conflict-Affected Communities in Ukraine and Provision of Financial Assistance to Address Essential Needs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The invasion of Ukraine on 24 February resulted in the displacement of nearly 6.3 million people as of 23 June 2022, according to round 6 of the IOM Displacement Report. The overall scale and unpredictability of the situation requires immediate humanitarian assistance for the most vulnerable displaced and conflict-affected communities. Through this project, IOM is providing specialized protection services, community-based activities aiming to raise awareness, as well as capacity building activities for partners, government, community leaders and other relevant persons.</narrative>
  </description>
